# muga.app response headers — Cloudflare Pages.
#
# The site is served by the Cloudflare Pages project "muga-landing", whose
# build output directory is `landing/`. This file is the ONLY place response
# headers are configured: there is no Worker in front of it. Pages applies the
# file on the NEXT deployment, so a change here is not live until main is
# pushed and the build finishes.
#
# Verify after any change to this file, because a rule that does not match
# fails silently — nothing errors, the header is simply absent:
#
#   curl -sD - -o /dev/null https://muga.app/ | grep -i content-security-policy
#   curl -sD - -o /dev/null https://muga.app/clean/ui.js | grep -i cache-control
#
# CSP audit (landing/index.html, landing/clean/index.html):
#   - Styles: one <style> block per page, static, no user data.
#   - Scripts: inline blocks (backronym rotator, console easter egg, the lazy
#     tool bootstrap) plus same-origin ES modules under /clean/.
#   - External origins, and there are only three: images and icons from
#     rules.muga.app, the Archivo + IBM Plex Mono stylesheet from
#     fonts.googleapis.com, and the font files that stylesheet pulls from
#     fonts.gstatic.com.
#   - 'unsafe-inline' is required for both style-src and script-src: the pages
#     have no build step and no nonce/hash injection. They carry no
#     user-controlled data, so the risk is accepted for a static site.
#   - No eval, no external scripts, no frames.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' https://rules.muga.app data:; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000

# Pages serves HTML with max-age=0 but static assets with max-age=14400, so a
# deploy can hand a browser the new /clean page against a four-hour-old engine.
# /clean is a contract: index.html, ui.js and the vendored engine bundle only
# agree when they ship together (#1082). Force the rest to revalidate too.

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*.mjs
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
